      "notes": "The common myna thrives in urban and suburban environments; in Canberra, 110 mynas released between 1968 and 1971 reached a population density of 75 birds per square kilometer by 1994. Nests in building cavities, roof spaces, and nest boxes; frequently forages on roadsides and in urban parks. Listed among the world's 100 worst invasive species by IUCN."
    }
